            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 553)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Someone can send you a whole session as one link.</b> Paste it into the Shared Review window and Asobi Review downloads the session, unpacks it and opens it — shots, notes and marks, ready to review. Your notes and markup go back to whoever sent it, because the same link joins you to their session.</li>
<li><b>Ask for a better version of a clip.</b> A delivery travels light so it arrives quickly. When you want to look properly at the clip you're on, <b>Request Higher-Resolution Clip</b> asks the sender's Asobi to re-encode that one clip at full size; it swaps in where it was, keeping your notes and marks. A percentage shows how far along it is.</li>
<li><b>You choose where delivered sessions are kept.</b> Settings ▸ <b>Session bundles location</b> — put them on whichever disk suits, rather than your home folder.</li>
<li><b>Pasted review links work properly</b>, including the short ones, and they name you — so your seat, your watermark and your notes are yours.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
